{"version": 2, "id": "g4b-steel-blocks", "name": "Cardboard lets the pull through, steel blocks it", "seconds": 2.0, "release": 0.3, "stage": {"x0": -0.56, "x1": 3.19, "y0": -0.16, "y1": 2.34}, "items": [{"id": "table", "type": "table", "x": 1.3, "y": 0}, {"id": "m1", "type": "bar-magnet", "name": "Magnet 1", "x": 0.8, "y": 0.0095, "fixed": true, "props": {}}, {"id": "card", "type": "barrier-sheet", "name": "Cardboard", "x": 0.883, "y": 0.0, "props": {"material": "cardboard"}}, {"id": "clip1", "type": "paper-clip", "name": "Clip behind cardboard", "x": 0.908, "y": 0.0005, "props": {}}, {"id": "m2", "type": "bar-magnet", "name": "Magnet 2", "x": 1.8, "y": 0.0095, "fixed": true, "props": {}}, {"id": "steel", "type": "barrier-sheet", "name": "Steel sheet", "x": 1.883, "y": 0.0, "props": {"material": "steel"}}, {"id": "clip2", "type": "paper-clip", "name": "Clip behind steel", "x": 1.908, "y": 0.0005, "props": {}}], "goals": [{"kind": "sticks", "item": "clip1", "to": "card"}, {"kind": "not_attracted", "source": "m2", "item": "clip2"}], "notes": "Two ceramic bars on the table, a sheet standing 8 mm past each north pole and a clip lying 8 mm behind it: through cardboard the clip slides up to the sheet; a 0.5 mm steel sheet takes the field into itself (most of a ceramic pole's), so its clip stays put (3-PS2-3)."},
{"version": 2, "id": "g7b-compass-flip-level", "name": "A magnet turned around level with a compass turns its needle around", "seconds": 3.0, "release": 0.3, "stage": {"x0": -0.56, "x1": 3.19, "y0": -0.16, "y1": 2.34}, "items": [{"id": "table", "type": "table", "x": 1.3, "y": 0}, {"id": "magnet", "type": "bar-magnet", "name": "Bar magnet", "x": 1.0, "y": 0.033, "fixed": true, "props": {"flip": true}}, {"id": "c", "type": "compass", "name": "Compass", "x": 1.175, "y": 0.033, "props": {}}], "goals": [{"kind": "points", "compass": "c", "angle_deg": 180}], "notes": "The compass 10 cm from the bar's end, on its axis: the bar flipped (south pole toward the compass) turns the needle round to point at it (180\u00b0); the needle starts pointing exactly away from that field, a balance no real needle keeps."},
