{"version": 2, "id": "g13b-ping-pong", "name": "A rubbed balloon rolls a ping-pong ball", "seconds": 3.0, "release": 0.3, "stage": {"x0": -0.56, "x1": 3.19, "y0": -0.16, "y1": 2.34}, "items": [{"id": "table", "type": "table", "x": 1.3, "y": 0}, {"id": "balloon", "type": "balloon", "name": "Balloon", "x": 1.0, "y": 0.127, "props": {"rubbed": 10, "rubbed_side": "lower right", "thread": 0.3}}, {"id": "ball", "type": "ping-pong-ball", "name": "Ping-pong ball", "x": 1.105, "y": 0.02, "props": {}}], "goals": [{"kind": "attracts", "source": "balloon", "item": "ball"}], "notes": "A plastic (celluloid) shell is polarized only as a dielectric (\u03b5_r 3.5): it rolls to the rubbed patch from about half a centimetre, where an aluminium can goes from several centimetres."},
